
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>Introduction to Bootstrap</title>

    <!-- Bootstrap CSS CDN -->
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"
          rel="stylesheet">

    <style>
        body {
            background-color: #f4f6f9;
        }

        .hero {
            background-color: #712cf9;
            color: white;
            padding: 60px 20px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .topic-card {
            border: none;
            border-radius: 12px;
            transition: transform 0.3s;
        }

        .topic-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-5px);
        }

        footer {
            background-color: #212529;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 20px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <!-- Navigation Bar -->
    <nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-dark bg-dark">
        <div class="container">

            <a class="navbar-brand" href="#">Learn Bootstrap</a>

            <button class="navbar-toggler" type="button"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#navbarMenu">

                <span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span>
            </button>

            <div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarMenu">

                <ul class="navbar-nav ms-auto">
                    <li class="nav-item">
                        <a class="nav-link" href="#what">What is Bootstrap?</a>
                    </li>

                    <li class="nav-item">
                        <a class="nav-link" href="#why">Why Bootstrap?</a>
                    </li>

                    <li class="nav-item">
                        <a class="nav-link" href="#mobile">Mobile-First</a>
                    </li>

                    <li class="nav-item">
                        <a class="nav-link" href="#apply">How to Apply</a>
                    </li>
                </ul>

            </div>
        </div>
    </nav>


    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <header class="hero">
        <div class="container">

            <h1>Introduction to Bootstrap</h1>

            <p class="lead">
                Learn how to create responsive and modern websites
                using the Bootstrap framework.
            </p>

            <a href="#what" class="btn btn-light btn-lg">
                Start Learning
            </a>

        </div>
    </header>


    <!-- Main Content -->
    <main class="container my-5">

        <div class="row g-4">

            <!-- Topic 1 -->
            <div class="col-12" id="what">

                <div class="card topic-card shadow-sm p-4">

                    <h2 class="text-primary">
                        1. What is Bootstrap Framework?
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        Bootstrap is a free, open-source CSS framework
                        used to create responsive and mobile-friendly
                        websites.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        It provides ready-made components such as:
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>Buttons</li>
                        <li>Navigation bars</li>
                        <li>Cards</li>
                        <li>Forms</li>
                        <li>Tables</li>
                        <li>Responsive grids</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Bootstrap helps developers build websites
                        faster without writing all CSS from scratch.
                    </p>

                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Topic 2 -->
            <div class="col-12" id="why">

                <div class="card topic-card shadow-sm p-4">

                    <h2 class="text-success">
                        2. Why Bootstrap?
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        Bootstrap is popular because it makes
                        web development easier and faster.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>Easy to learn and use.</li>
                        <li>Responsive design for different devices.</li>
                        <li>Ready-made design components.</li>
                        <li>Consistent appearance across browsers.</li>
                        <li>Saves time when developing websites.</li>
                        <li>Customizable using CSS.</li>
                    </ul>

                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Topic 3 -->
            <div class="col-12" id="mobile">

                <div class="card topic-card shadow-sm p-4">

                    <h2 class="text-danger">
                        3. What is Mobile-First Strategy?
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        Mobile-First is a web design strategy where
                        developers design a website for mobile devices
                        first and then adapt it for larger screens.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Bootstrap uses a mobile-first grid system.
                    </p>

                    <h5>Example:</h5>

                    <div class="row text-center g-2">

                        <div class="col-12 col-md-4">
                            <div class="bg-primary text-white p-3 rounded">
                                Mobile
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="col-12 col-md-4">
                            <div class="bg-success text-white p-3 rounded">
                                Tablet
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="col-12 col-md-4">
                            <div class="bg-warning text-dark p-3 rounded">
                                Desktop
                            </div>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                    <p class="mt-3">
                        The columns appear vertically on small screens
                        and horizontally on medium and larger screens.
                    </p>

                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Topic 4 -->
            <div class="col-12" id="apply">

                <div class="card topic-card shadow-sm p-4">

                    <h2 class="text-info">
                        4. How to Apply Bootstrap to Applications?
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        Bootstrap can be added to an HTML application
                        using a CDN link.
                    </p>

                    <h5>Step 1: Add Bootstrap CSS</h5>

                    <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded"><code>&lt;link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"
rel="stylesheet"&gt;</code></pre>

                    <h5>Step 2: Use Bootstrap classes</h5>

                    <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded"><code>&lt;button class="btn btn-primary"&gt;
    Click Me
&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>

                    <h5>Step 3: Add Bootstrap JavaScript</h5>

                    <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded"><code>&lt;script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>

                    <p>
                        Now you can use Bootstrap components and
                        utilities in your application.
                    </p>

                    <button class="btn btn-primary">
                        Example Bootstrap Button
                    </button>

                </div>
            </div>

        </div>

    </main>


    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer>
        <p class="mb-0">
            Introduction to Bootstrap | Learn Web Development
        </p>
    </footer>


    <!-- Bootstrap JavaScript CDN -->
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>

</body>
</html>
